<section class="marketing-section marketing-explainer" id="what-is-quotation-software">
  <div class="marketing-section-head">
    <h2>What Is Foreign Trade Quotation Software?</h2>
    <p class="marketing-section-intro">A practical explanation for export-focused sales operations.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="marketing-explainer-summary">
    Foreign trade quotation software helps B2B export teams control revisions, improve buyer visibility, and run faster quote follow-ups without heavy ERP overhead.
  </p>
  <ul class="marketing-explainer-keypoints">
    <li>Replaces fragmented spreadsheets and attachments with one structured quote workflow.</li>
    <li>Supports quote revision control and buyer-facing live links in daily sales execution.</li>
    <li>Keeps export quotation management practical with professional PDF/Excel output.</li>
  </ul>

  <details class="marketing-explainer-details">
    <summary>Read full explanation</summary>

    <h3>Why Export Teams Need It</h3>
    <p>
      Foreign trade quotation software is the execution layer between lead discussions and final buyer confirmation in international sales.
    </p>
    <p>
      For B2B export teams, quoting is not just document creation. It is revision management, buyer communication, and follow-up control inside one commercial workflow.
    </p>

    <h3>Why Spreadsheet Quoting Breaks at Scale</h3>
    <p>
      Many teams start with spreadsheets, email threads, and attachment chains. That can work early, but volume quickly creates version confusion.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>No single source of truth when quotes move across teammates.</li>
      <li>Revision history gets fragmented across files and messages.</li>
      <li>Buyers compare old attachments instead of the latest offer.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What a Practical Quotation CRM Should Do</h3>
    <p>
      Excel remains useful for analysis, but it is weak for live export quotation management. ERP can provide deep governance, yet many exporters find it too heavy for frontline quoting speed.
    </p>
    <p>
      Teams need a balanced quotation CRM workflow: fast for daily negotiation, structured for reliable internal execution.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Track revisions clearly and keep every version visible.</li>
      <li>Share one buyer-facing live quote link to prevent confusion.</li>
      <li>Export professional PDF/Excel files without extra manual work.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Rubusoo is built for that exact gap. It gives B2B export teams clearer buyer communication, fewer avoidable errors, and stronger follow-up discipline across the quote lifecycle.
    </p>
  </details>
</section>

